{"title":"KGS math club/solution 10 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The coefficient of the tangent can be found from implicit derivative formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a45f689a2eb21e91f4b18b237e3852bf83d7161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dy / dx = - (dz / dx) / (dz / dy) = - (2x + y) / (2y + x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"395\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7848d0033820699133730ff389591c7050833a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = x^2 + y^2 + x y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So we want to find a pair (x, y) such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d373d7813ec1d70c21c8594847cdbe3357f2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 + x y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p><p>and  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bab1dbf24cfa53006cd5fea3c38207f0e8f7b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y - 2) / x = - (2x + y) / (2y + x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d008c30b438e0b88e947acc85ae78a21c3e532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;=&gt; 2 y^2 + (x - 4 + x) y - 2 x + 2 x^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af9f761452a4812ce7eff1da30643b9ee9ecbf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;=&gt; y^2 + x y - 2 y - x + x^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Substituting the first to the second, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/479ac5680210bade558b0b2667fb70b340faf1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y^2 + x y + x^2) - 2 y - x = 1 - 2 y - x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"326\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb473609435dd20d822217d007e346e967b8e95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;=&gt; y = (1 - x) / 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Substituting this back to the first equation, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2607d3cbe901261ef0cad289ea106c63afe8f1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (1 - x)^2 / 4 + x (1 - x) / 2 - 1 = (1 + 1/4 - 1/2) x^2 + (-1/2 + 1/2) x + (1/4 - 1) = 3/4 x^2 - 3/4 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"808\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b66f216026a5d8347b1ec6aff86c2a5935e8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;=&gt; x = +-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We have thus found two solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07ebc9af627a4aa807543cf349f9ad8301c0fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y) = (1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f004a9917828a28718276d021ed466f6f1254c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y) = (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Verification: \n</p><p>at (-1, 1), the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70dc9f8170f134184e2158fe37e3a02d9001a0eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dy / dx = - (-2 + 1) / (2 - 1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />, so the tangent goes from (-1, 1) to (0, 2)\n</p><p>at (1, 0), the  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac8002975ca7cd89a7f54be8e7776cb47a49fb3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dy / dx = -(2 + 0) / (0 + 1) = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"254\" height=\"20\" />, so the tangent goes from (1, 0) to (0, 2)\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175646\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 43/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2907/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8879:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175646 and revision id 35623. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}